{"id":106630,"title":"here","url":"https://github.com/Donitzo/three.js-volume-renderer","final_url":"https://codeload.github.com/Donitzo/three.js-volume-renderer/tar.gz/HEAD","year":2025,"kind":"link","source":"link","doi":null,"arxiv":null,"sha256":"664f7df39d8843bcfaccc2a2cbb9e55e11d09460fb71645c1d53051d22828a3c","ctype":"application/gzip","text_src":"repo","fetched_at":1793234056.9351635,"text_chars":237813,"abstract":"Github\n\nhttps://github.com › Donitzo › three.js-volume-renderer\n\nthree.js Volume Renderer - GitHub\nAt each step along the ray, we sample volume data (e.g. density, extinction coefficient, distance function) and accumulate it (e.g., via alpha blending or by estimating a mean value) until the ray exits the volume. Unlike surface-based raymarchers that stop at the first hit, this approach processes the entire volume along the ray.","file":null,"marks":["unofficial"],"links":["https://codeload.github.com/Donitzo/three.js-volume-renderer/tar.gz/HEAD","https://github.com/Donitzo/three.js-volume-renderer"],"cited_by":[{"path":"1327-signed-distance-field-from-mesh.md","name":"Signed Distance Field from Mesh","k":5},{"path":"2789-transfer-function-and-opacity-mapping.md","name":"Transfer Function and Opacity Mapping","k":3},{"path":"2788-ray-marching-and-discretization.md","name":"Ray Marching and Discretization","k":5},{"path":"7158-3d-volume-atlas-packing.md","name":"3D Volume Atlas Packing","k":1},{"path":"7157-volume-atlas-texture-update.md","name":"Volume Atlas Texture Update","k":1},{"path":"7164-3d-atlas-texture-creation.md","name":"3D Atlas Texture Creation","k":1},{"path":"7156-custom-volume-sampling-via-glsl-injection.md","name":"Custom Volume Sampling via GLSL Injection","k":1},{"path":"7159-mesh-sdf-sampling.md","name":"Mesh SDF Sampling","k":1},{"path":"4877-ray-marching-volume-rendering.md","name":"Ray Marching Volume Rendering","k":14},{"path":"7856-signed-distance-field-sampler-from-mesh.md","name":"Signed Distance Field Sampler from Me